    <briefdescription>
<para>REST controller for appointment records of the appointment-providing entities. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A {entityType} path segment (clinics, pharmacies, laboratories, radiologycenters) selects a concrete <ref refid="classAppointmentController" kindref="compound">AppointmentController&lt;T&gt;</ref> from a std::variant registry. Every handler builds a callback that maps the controller&apos;s numeric status to a standard JSON HTTP response and constructs a <ref refid="structRequester" kindref="compound">Requester</ref> from the &quot;clientID&quot;/&quot;clientGroup&quot; attributes inserted by the Auth filter, so all routes are SECURE. When DatabaseConfig::async is set the *Async controller methods are awaited in a drogon::Task coroutine; otherwise executeControllerMethod runs the blocking permission check and query on the shared <ref refid="classDbExecutor" kindref="compound">DbExecutor</ref>. Controllers and the executor are shared service-locator objects. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
